{
  "map_version": 4,
  "__readme": [
    "Legacy config.json key mapping. Applied automatically every time a config",
    "is loaded (local open or SFTP download), BEFORE template migration. Every",
    "change appears in the migration dialog and audit log. Edit + Reload Key",
    "Map (App Config tab) - no application rebuild needed.",
    "",
    "Processing order: sections -> properties -> auto-normalization ->",
    "value_map -> moves -> unused-device removal -> connection_fields ->",
    "removals -> carriage returns -> device defaults -> companion_keys ->",
    "defaults.",
    "",
    "connection_fields: com_type -> the properties a device on that connection",
    "  must NOT have. A serial device has no ip_address/net_port/protocol/",
    "  password/user, so those are dropped; one that held a real value is",
    "  logged as a CONFLICT first rather than vanishing silently.",
    "removals: properties dropped on convert. 'key_match' is a whole-name",
    "  regex, optional 'section' is a '*' wildcard (default: every section,",
    "  plus stray scalars at the root). Add 'when_key' (SECTION.key) and",
    "  'when_value_in' to gate the removal on another key - the power outlet",
    "  rule only fires when dev_power_controllers says there is no controller.",
    "  A rule whose gating key is absent never fires.",
    "",
    "remove_unused_devices + device_counts: legacy device blocks whose family",
    "  count says they're not in use (No / 0 / above the count) are REMOVED",
    "  instead of converted. Only blocks renamed from legacy section names are",
    "  eligible, so new-style template files keep every block.",
    "",
    "",
    "auto_case_normalization: when true, a legacy property automatically",
    "  renames to any current key that matches after lowercasing and removing",
    "  underscores (e.g. Output_Proj1 -> output_proj_1, GVE_BLDG -> gve_bldg,",
    "  COMTYPE -> com_type). Explicit 'properties' entries always win.",
    "sections: top-level renames. 'match' is a whole-name regex; $1..$9",
    "  insert capture groups.",
    "properties: flat OLDNAME -> new_name map applied inside every section.",
    "value_map: per-property value normalization AFTER rename. New values keep",
    "  their JSON type ('True' -> true, 'Yes' -> '1').",
    "moves: relocate a property to another section, e.g. the legacy SYSTEM",
    "  per-device GVE IDs into each device block's gve_id.",
    "defaults: per section family (wildcard *), keys injected only when",
    "  missing. '{n}' becomes the device number. Existing values are never",
    "  overwritten.",
    "Keys starting with '__' anywhere are ignored (use them for comments).",
    "",
    "escape_carriage_returns: real CR/CRLF control characters in string values",
    "  become the two-character backslash+r sequence in memory. The JSON",
    "  encoder escapes the backslash on save, so the config.json ON DISK",
    "  contains \\\\r ('Intake<CR><LF>Fans' -> \"Intake\\\\rFans\" in the saved",
    "  file) - the new style the processor code reads.",
    "companion_keys: for every property matching key_match, ensure_key (with",
    "  $1..$9 capture groups) is created in the same section when missing,",
    "  set to 'value'. E.g. every converted power1_outlet_N gets a matching",
    "  power1_outlet_N_supports_reboot. Existing values are never overwritten.",
    "device_labels + device_templates: legacy device blocks get a generated",
    "  name '<Label> - <model>' (numbered only when the family has multiple",
    "  units), btn_name/lbl_name from the same-numbered template block, and",
    "  module/keep_alive_trigger from a template block with a matching model."
  ],
  "auto_case_normalization": true,
  "remove_unused_devices": true,
  "device_counts": {
    "__comment": "SYSTEM_SETUP count key -> device prefix, used by remove_unused_devices. Legacy blocks numbered above the count (or in families set to No/0) are dropped instead of converted. Only applies to blocks renamed from legacy names.",
    "dev_cameras": "CAMERADEVICE_",
    "dev_projectors": "PROJECTORDEVICE_",
    "dev_switchers": "SWITCHERDEVICE_",
    "dev_dsps": "DSPDEVICE_",
    "dev_usb_switchers": "USBDEVICE_",
    "dev_media_ports": "MEDIAPORTDEVICE_",
    "dev_wireless": "WIRELESSDEVICE_",
    "dev_recorders": "RECORDERDEVICE_",
    "dev_screens": "SCREENDEVICE_",
    "dev_power_controllers": "POWERDEVICE_"
  },
  "escape_carriage_returns": true,
  "connection_fields": {
    "__comment": "Keyed by com_type (after value_map normalizes it): the properties a device on that connection must NOT carry. Removed on convert; one that held a real value is reported as a CONFLICT first so nothing disappears quietly. device_id and keep_alive_trigger are deliberately NOT listed - they describe the module, not the link. The reverse direction (serial_port / baud on a device that never opens a COM port) is also enforced live in the editor by the 'hideWhen' entries on those keys in ui_schema.json.",
    "serial": [
      "ip_address",
      "net_port",
      "protocol",
      "service_port",
      "password",
      "user"
    ],
    "network": [
      "serial_port",
      "baud"
    ],
    "serialoverethernet": [
      "serial_port",
      "baud"
    ],
    "http": [
      "serial_port",
      "baud"
    ]
  },
  "removals": [
    {
      "__comment": "Superseded by the METRICS_CONFIG block.",
      "key_match": "api_proxy_server",
      "reason": "superseded by METRICS_CONFIG"
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Generic room label; the room identity lives in gve_bldg + gve_room.",
      "key_match": "ROOM",
      "reason": "room identity comes from gve_bldg + gve_room"
    },
    {
      "__comment": "A device's GVE id belongs in that device's own block, the way every other device already does it. This SYSTEM_SETUP copy is from an older build; WIRELESSDEVICE_n.gve_id is the one to fill in.",
      "key_match": "gve_id_wireless_.*",
      "reason": "the wireless device's gve_id lives in its own block"
    },
    {
      "__comment": "Recorded for a wake-on-LAN feature that was never built; no ControlScript template reads it.",
      "key_match": "pcmac",
      "reason": "unused - no template reads it"
    },
    {
      "__comment": "With no power controller in the room the outlet names and their actions are dead data. Fires only when dev_power_controllers actually says none - a missing count never triggers it.",
      "key_match": "power1_outlet_.*",
      "when_key": "SYSTEM_SETUP.dev_power_controllers",
      "when_value_in": [ "0", "no", "false", "" ],
      "reason": "no power controller in this room"
    }
  ],
  "companion_keys": [
    {
      "__comment": "Each outlet that survives gets its reboot capability flags, so a room with a power controller carries them for every outlet it actually has. Defaults match the template: reboot supported, not reboot-only. These two are the whole story - the old power1_outlet_N_action key was a third way of saying reboot-only and is stripped on load, see foldOutletActionIntoRebootOnly.",
      "key_match": "power1_outlet_(\\d+)$",
      "ensure_key": "power1_outlet_$1_supports_reboot",
      "value": true
    },
    {
      "key_match": "power1_outlet_(\\d+)$",
      "ensure_key": "power1_outlet_$1_reboot_only",
      "value": false
    }
  ],
